{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened","id":1284949,"title":"Making a new Mage Setting (Anstruther Academy) for young Awakened","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-05T06:56:35-08:00","id":1284949,"title":"Making a new Mage Setting (Anstruther Academy) for young Awakened","content":"Anstruther Academy (pronounced Ainster if you're Scottish, Ans-tru-ther otherwise) was established in legend by one of the students of Merlin. Originally a Hermetic school which catered to a small number of talented children, it is now the Traditions' primary educational establishment for all Awakened children.<br /> <br /> The setting takes some inspiration from Hogwarts (Scottish location, magic school for children) but I intend for it to be &quot;what if the WoD had a magic school&quot; rather than &quot;what if Hogwarts were in the WoD&quot;. I really want to leave behind some of the worse aspects of the world-building like there being an Evil House or the school being modeled on private boarding schools etc.<br /> <br /> The school is a large castle which was the ancestral home of one of its founders. Various wards give it an Arcane rating and protect it from sleepers. The reality zone is pretty messy. All of the Traditions are represented to a certain degree, so there are modern religious sites and pagan stones (Scotland is full of those), laboratories and libraries...<br /> <br /> Rather than teachers being divided by subject, teachers are closer to mentors and are divided by style. Teaching teleportation to a room full of teenagers is pretty much pointless if none of them work with the Latin incantations you use. Some topics such as History (backstory of the Traditions etc) and Magickal Theory (here's what happens to Mages who mess around with X, here's why safety should always come first, here's an anecdote about how I escaped a situation without having to use my powers), Languages and various Skills/Knowledges are more universal, and are taught in large groups.<br /> <br /> The castle would be full of secrets and oddities to fuel many stories. Lost Grimoires, hidden chambers, powerful Wonders, Bygones like Dragons, gateways to other worlds created by reckless students, secret societies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-05-2019, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T07:30:54-08:00","id":1284963,"title":"","content":"Recruitment; the Traditions aren't hunting down every single child that Awakens and sending them off to a special school. To do that they'd need to be entirely fused with the Technocracy. The school is for awakened children who come to the attention of the Traditions, and a good proportion of the attendees are the biological relatives or mentees of Tradition mages.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, most Mages do awaken as adults and learn by themselves. The purpose of the school is to protect young vulnerable mages from the world, protect the world from them, and help them to grow into powerful agents of the Traditions. Some might label it an indoctrination camp.<br /> <br /> If a child has sleeper guardians, they are misled using magickal trickery and persuasion, and are convinced to send their &quot;gifted child&quot; to an elite and secretive school with no fee.<br /> <br /> It might be presumed that there is an inverse institution run by the Technocracy, since they are better able to perform such recruitment. There is no evidence that such an institution exists, but that's what you would expect...<br /> <br /> A lot of learning takes place outside of classrooms and is much more free-form than might be expected at an &quot;academy&quot;. Examinations are optional and allow for a variety of approaches; they are challenges which can be overcome through many different paths. A Verbena might spend their days and nights in the nearby wilderness, only checking with their teachers when they encounter problems. Meanwhile a Chorister might spend all their time cloistered in chapels and musical activities and libraries, being taught constantly by their mentors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-05-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T07:38:30-08:00","id":1284965,"title":"","content":"What styles are you thinking of? <br /> <br /> If this institution is that old, there is the very real possibility of lots of legacy departments and rules. There might be groups that are not Traditions (or never were), and even groups that don't exist anywhere else. Two ideas that come to mind:<br /> <br /> One of the members of House Tremere still teaches there. Yeah, yeah, traitorous vampires and all that, but he's got tenure. No one's even certain if he's a vampire or not, partly because he's deliberately keeping that a secret and partly because it's dangerous to look too closely into faculty secrets.<br /> <br /> The Cosians have a department there. They joined the school before their participation in the Order of Reason was official. Even though the Order of Reason has long since moved on in philosophy, longstanding agreements and traditions say they have to turn all of their students over to the Technocracy when they graduate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T07:41:20-08:00","id":1284966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1284965#post1284965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What styles are you thinking of?<br /> <br /> If this institution is that old, there is the very real possibility of lots of legacy departments and rules. There might be groups that are not Traditions (or never were), and even groups that don't exist anywhere else. Two ideas that come to mind:<br /> <br /> One of the members of House Tremere still teaches there. Yeah, yeah, traitorous vampires and all that, but he's got tenure. No one's even certain if he's a vampire or not, partly because he's deliberately keeping that a secret and partly because it's dangerous to look too closely into faculty secrets.<br /> <br /> The Cosians have a department there. They joined the school before their participation in the Order of Reason was official. Even though the Order of Reason has long since moved on in philosophy, longstanding agreements and traditions say they have to turn all of their students over to the Technocracy when they graduate.</div> </div> </div> </div>VAMPIRE PROFESSOR that's a glorious idea. I love it so much. Tremere holdover who coaches Mages in Certamen tactics. He could even be the head of one of the school's houses...<br /> <br /> While the idea of a &quot;yeah we have a weird treaty where we give them 2% of our students and they have their own special class&quot; is pretty neat and fitting for the world of Academia, it doesn't really mesh that well with the idea of it being a secret school. Plus I doubt the Technocracy want agents who have spent 7 years befriending reality deviants and learning about a more flexible view of enlightenment. It's just going to give you a nest of traitors pointing in both directions.<br /> <br /> Definitely thinking of an old establishment. Its lore claims that it stretches back to Arthurian times. No one is entirely sure since it's hard to perform sensitive Time magick in such a chaotic setting. In fact attempts to establish the school's origins have given multiple contradictory pasts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Getting rid of &quot;oh and there's splat and splat too&quot; since looking back it was turning into a kitchen sink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-05-2019, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T09:12:42-08:00","id":1284975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1284966#post1284966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> VAMPIRE PROFESSOR that's a glorious idea. I love it so much. I'm immediately integrating that. It would also make sense for the building to have a few Wraiths in residence, and the nearby woods should have some Werewolf presence because of the intensity of nodes/cairns. An Earthbound demon slumbering beneath the loch would also be quite fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't many better ways for Wraiths to escape the Hierarchy than hanging around a bunch of wizards. I could even see there being one or two who claim to be wizards -really, they've just been hanging around so long they are good at giving advice (they are effectively specialized libraries, not mentors)- who tutor students who agree to let them skinride along for a semester. They just have to avoid the Chakravanti wing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the idea of a &quot;yeah we have a weird treaty where we give them 2% of our students and they have their own special class&quot; is pretty neat and fitting for the world of Academia, it doesn't really mesh that well with the idea of it being a secret school. Plus I doubt the Technocracy want agents who have spent 7 years befriending reality deviants and learning about a more flexible view of enlightenment. It's just going to give you a nest of traitors pointing in both directions. </div> </div> </div>The other way of running it is the faculty keeps finding unique exceptions not to. Behind the scenes the Cosian Faculty and the Administration is adamantly against turning anyone over, but they can't openly admit that because that would tarnish the university's integrity. So instead they let the students (and many of the other departments) think that they will turn young cosians over, but they find ever more complicated and arcane reasons not to (or let the students engage in daring midnight escapes just after graduation, that works too). <br /> <br /> Or not. Honestly, the most recent magical university game I've been in was a Pigsmoke one shot, so I may be a little over-focused on bizarre faculty politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T09:29:13-08:00","id":1284982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1284975#post1284975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There aren't many better ways for Wraiths to escape the Hierarchy than hanging around a bunch of wizards. I could even see there being one or two who claim to be wizards -really, they've just been hanging around so long they are good at giving advice (they are effectively specialized libraries, not mentors)- who tutor students who agree to let them skinride along for a semester. They just have to avoid the Chakravanti wing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wraiths of old Mages would be an amazing resource, especially since some magickal traditions prefer resources other than books. And yeah it's a cozy haunt since Spirit magick can fix most of a Wraith's problems.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if you're going to be teaching people how to channel ghosts or commune with the dead, it's good to have some ghosts hanging around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T12:50:55-08:00","id":1285038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened#post1284949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than teachers being divided by subject, teachers are closer to mentors and are divided by style. Teaching teleportation to a room full of teenagers is pretty much pointless if none of them work with the Latin incantations you use. Some topics such as History (backstory of the Traditions etc) and Magickal Theory (here's what happens to Mages who mess around with X, here's why safety should always come first, here's an anecdote about how I escaped a situation without having to use my powers), Languages and various Skills/Knowledges are more universal, and are taught in large groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>That this school teaches for all the Traditions and several styles gives me an idea:<br /> <br /> This institution was founded not very long after the Great Convocation (albeit the place could be older, and perhaps the Tremere already resided here before it became a school) as an effort of cooperation similar to the First Cabal.<br /> <br /> The first Council understood that cooperating with mages of wildly different belief systems was going to be a challenge, to say the least. The First Cabal was a (rather unfortunate) symbol indicating that such cooperation was possible. The school was a bet on the future: Young mages living and learning together could develop an &quot;open&quot; Paradigm (that is a mage that has a preffered way of doing magick, but believes other Paradigms are valid too) and become a good element for future multi-tradition cabals.<br /> <br /> If this is the case the optimal way of teaching would be free classes with professors that are open to anyone that wants to learn (in adition to the basic learning in maths and language any child should have).<br /> <br /> Childhood and adolescence are stages of change. One can't expect a kid that's still learning her place in the world to hold to an unchanging Paradigm forever. The hardships and constant array of new experiences (like, say, sexuality) will mold and change their beliefs<br /> <br /> A traditionalist Hermetic may fall in love with a Dreamspeaker and bent her potent will to understand his spiritual heritage. A boy educated into hacker culture and science might find D&amp;D wizards enticing and want to learn how to do their magick stuff now that he knows it exists.<br /> <br /> This will cause problems with wizardly parents, but try as they might the parents won't be able to prevent this intermingling if all the young mages learn at the same place (unless potent magick it used, but then why send the children there in the first place?) because it's fully natural (not to mention a seed of stories/characters)<br /> <br /> And this is good for the school purposes. All young mages would learn basic magick theory, including the &quot;nine spheres&quot; for inter-tradition comunication purposes. Other than that the children would be encouraged to try as many fields as they like, speaking with tutors of several orientations and entering in classes, even if they may not understand everything, in order to entice their curiosity and expand their Paradigm (and, perhaps in secret, to foster the &quot;we're all god(s) in disguise&quot; Paradigm that the Trads try to push on the world). Graduates would excel at syncretism and doing rituals with mages of other traditions, which may not be of the likes of every Traditionalist but does foster the goals of the Traditions as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-05-2019, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T03:04:16-08:00","id":1285178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285038#post1285038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That this school teaches for all the Traditions and several styles gives me an idea:<br /> <br /> This institution was founded not very long after the Great Convocation (albeit the place could be older, and perhaps the Tremere already resided here before it became a school) as an effort of cooperation similar to the First Cabal.<br /> <br /> The first Council understood that cooperating with mages of wildly different belief systems was going to be a challenge, to say the least. The First Cabal was a (rather unfortunate) symbol indicating that such cooperation was possible. The school was a bet on the future: Young mages living and learning together could develop an &quot;open&quot; Paradigm (that is a mage that has a preffered way of doing magick, but believes other Paradigms are valid too) and become a good element for future multi-tradition cabals.<br /> <br /> If this is the case the optimal way of teaching would be free classes with professors that are open to anyone that wants to learn (in adition to the basic learning in maths and language any child should have).<br /> <br /> Childhood and adolescence are stages of change. One can't expect a kid that's still learning her place in the world to hold to an unchanging Paradigm forever. The hardships and constant array of new experiences (like, say, sexuality) will mold and change their beliefs<br /> <br /> A traditionalist Hermetic may fall in love with a Dreamspeaker and bent her potent will to understand his spiritual heritage. A boy educated into hacker culture and science might find D&amp;D wizards enticing and want to learn how to do their magick stuff now that he knows it exists.<br /> <br /> This will cause problems with wizardly parents, but try as they might the parents won't be able to prevent this intermingling if all the young mages learn at the same place (unless potent magick it used, but then why send the children there in the first place?) because it's fully natural (not to mention a seed of stories/characters)<br /> <br /> And this is good for the school purposes. All young mages would learn basic magick theory, including the &quot;nine spheres&quot; for inter-tradition comunication purposes. Other than that the children would be encouraged to try as many fields as they like, speaking with tutors of several orientations and entering in classes, even if they may not understand everything, in order to entice their curiosity and expand their Paradigm (and, perhaps in secret, to foster the &quot;we're all god(s) in disguise&quot; Paradigm that the Trads try to push on the world). Graduates would excel at syncretism and doing rituals with mages of other traditions, which may not be of the likes of every Traditionalist but does foster the goals of the Traditions as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! Liking all of this. The castle having once been a haunt of House Tremere could be a great potential origin. Since it's a very magical place I've decided that it should have multiple competing origins which people can't agree over. Not sure that unfortunate historical symbols are the best addition but the rest of this is really well thought.<br /> <br /> Syncretism being the specialty of graduates is a really great idea! And I love the idea of paradigms evolving with time. Characters will arrive with Arete 1 and Paradigms which aren't fully defined yet. One PC has said that her Mage will have Awakened when she tried to get a Creepypasta ritual to work. Now her Avatar is a creepy forum poster, but she doesn't realize that their posts are only visible to her. With time she could evolve into a Virtual Adept or a Euthanatos mage, or anything inbetween. Another PC was saying he wants his guy to start off as a self-aggrandizing Edgelord who thinks he's the chosen one etc. and while he'll start off as a strict Hermetic he may loosen up with time.<br /> <br /> And yes I can imagine the school being VERY strict about Mage relatives/guardians interfering at the school. Helicopter parenting is not allowed ;-) Just let the kids develop their magick however they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:29:01-08:00","id":1285213,"title":"","content":"Story hook ideas...<br /> <br /> - Friendly NPC is losing control of their powers and doing everything they can to hide it. Their sanity is slipping and they're a young Marauder prodigy waiting to happen. How do the PCs handle this? Who do they tell about it?<br /> <br /> - Antagonistic and bullying behaviour culminates in a PC and an aggressive NPC peer agreeing to settle their differences through Certamen.<br /> <br /> - An ill-advised midnight summoning leads to dangerous results.<br /> <br /> - The master of a faculty announces a competition to create the most wondrous magickal display possible, with a grand prize for the winning group.<br /> <br /> - With most of the faculty absent, the academy's nodes are thrown into chaos by a mysterious force. Explosions of magickal energy begin to manifest along with spiritual chaos. The small group of students who are in residence over the vacation are left to mitigate the catastrophe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:58:20-08:00","id":1285221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285213#post1285213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Story hook ideas...<br /> <br /> - Antagonistic and bullying behaviour culminates in a PC and an aggressive NPC peer agreeing to settle their differences through Certamen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonus points if there is a short character arc of the characters having to figure out what the hell Certamen is supposed to be since the &quot;official&quot; description doesn't make much sense in their paradigm. &quot;Manifest a sphere as a sword, what does that even mean? Next you'll be telling me to manifest my Philosophy 209 course as a pair of boots.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - An ill-advised midnight summoning leads to dangerous results. </div> </div> </div>Or as I like to call it, Tuesday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - With most of the faculty absent, the academy's nodes are thrown into chaos by a mysterious force. Explosions of magickal energy begin to manifest along with spiritual chaos. The small group of students who are in residence over the vacation are left to mitigate the catastrophe. </div> </div> </div>Ho ho ho.<br /> <br /> Edit: On a more serious note, the holidays would be an excellent time for the shifters in the woods to mount an attack. Mages and Werewolves trying to use the same nodes/caerns is an explosion just waiting to happen. Or if you want to keep relations generally cordial between the two, it is an excellent time for a young pack to accidentally chase after a bane onto school grounds then try to take it down without being detected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-06-2019, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T08:54:11-08:00","id":1285259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285221#post1285221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bonus points if there is a short character arc of the characters having to figure out what the hell Certamen is supposed to be since the &quot;official&quot; description doesn't make much sense in their paradigm. &quot;Manifest a sphere as a sword, what does that even mean? Next you'll be telling me to manifest my Philosophy 209 course as a pair of boots.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I can imagine a VA having to hunt down an older VA student who has &quot;ported&quot; Certamen over into their understanding.<br /> <br /> &quot;Basically it's where you literally push your programming capacity RIGHT out of your body and manifest hard light holograms to duel people with. Hermetics don't really understand what they're doing and have a bunch of mystic gibberish about willpower instead. And yes, there is a manga which basically has Certamen in a digital world as its premise, I can lend it to you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T08:55:40-08:00","id":1285260,"title":"","content":"At the recommendation of a friend who is a Mage ST, I've decided to make the setting's resonance dangerously powerful and chaotically varied. Freak weather events, weird flora and fauna, strange spiritual fluctuations, a really messy local Middle Umbra, people getting out of bed and finding themselves in the middle of the lake in their PJs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T09:54:37-08:00","id":1285272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285260#post1285260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the recommendation of a friend who is a Mage ST, I've decided to make the setting's resonance dangerously powerful and chaotically varied. Freak weather events, weird flora and fauna, strange spiritual fluctuations, a really messy local Middle Umbra, people getting out of bed and finding themselves in the middle of the lake in their PJs...</div> </div> </div> </div>This school is going to be confirmation of every negative stereotype the wolves have about Mages isn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, one more idea, one of the groundskeepers is an actual Paradox spirit. No convoluted faculty politics is responsible for this one, he's not actually on the books and everyone would get rid of him if they could. They can't. They can't even talk about him because it draws his attention. Perhaps he's tied into the multiple histories of the school. Perhaps he's in all of them, but not at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:03:07-08:00","id":1285299,"title":"","content":"A Paradox spirit would be a good bogeyman for the children.<br /> <br /> Since Reality it's so chaotic in the premises of the school it's possible that the whole place it's at risk of getting send to the Umbra ( the same as the Lands of Giants, Lemuria and many other fantastical places), and the groundkeeper it's the one that has been sent by the Universe to decide when too much it's too much.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the all important subject of Paradox, something that all the children should learn about sooner rather than latter. And, of course, the spirit doesn't see with good eyes when children break the already <i>very </i>streched Reality of the school, and has no qualms imparting his own lessons on the subject...<br /> <br /> A humble mage (I imagine a Dreamspeaker), expert in Paradox and spirits, has the big responsability of appeasing the spirit so the school doesn't get send to the other side, and to help the children when they get in trouble with the groundkeeper","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-06-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:37:25-08:00","id":1285320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285272#post1285272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This school is going to be confirmation of every negative stereotype the wolves have about Mages isn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, one more idea, one of the groundskeepers is an actual Paradox spirit. No convoluted faculty politics is responsible for this one, he's not actually on the books and everyone would get rid of him if they could. They can't. They can't even talk about him because it draws his attention. Perhaps he's tied into the multiple histories of the school. Perhaps he's in all of them, but not at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love that. A janitor/handyman/custodian/groundsman guy who seems to pop up everywhere and none of the teachers talk about. He's a boon to the school really, since a good bit of Justice is thrown in there. If you keep messing up the school with magick detention is the LEAST of your worries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:41:35-08:00","id":1285323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285299#post1285299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Paradox spirit would be a good bogeyman for the children.<br /> <br /> Since Reality it's so chaotic in the premises of the school it's possible that the whole place it's at risk of getting send to the Umbra ( the same as the Lands of Giants, Lemuria and many other fantastical places), and the groundkeeper it's the one that has been sent by the Universe to decide when too much it's too much.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the all important subject of Paradox, something that all the children should learn about sooner rather than latter. And, of course, the spirit doesn't see with good eyes when children break the already <i>very </i>streched Reality of the school, and has no qualms imparting his own lessons on the subject...<br /> <br /> A humble mage (I imagine a Dreamspeaker), expert in Paradox and spirits, has the big responsability of appeasing the spirit so the school doesn't get send to the other side, and to help the children when they get in trouble with the groundkeeper</div> </div> </div> </div>So the universe is turning a blind eye to the school, partly because of its Arcane rating. If the magick that fuels the academy's obfuscation were to fail then the entire place would quickly experience what Douglas Adams called &quot;a critical failure to exist&quot;. The school doesn't bother Sleepers one bit since it naturally keeps them away from the castle itself and details and information about the castle just tend to slip out of people's minds. We're talking Arcane 10 to outsiders, a great work and a half.<br /> <br /> This means that within the school's grounds the consensus is juuuuuuust about ticking over, since witnesses aren't a problem. However the resonance is very volatile and it's not exactly peachy either, hence ol' Justin Ice (I'm not always the king of subtlety) the custodian being so irate.<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining a PC realizing he's a spirit using Spirit 1 and then trying to use Spirit 2 to control him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-06-2019, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T06:46:19-08:00","id":1285544,"title":"","content":"Ahh...that's SO not going to work well for the student. And not only because Spirit 2 doesn't allow much control. The thing with Paradox Spirits it's that you can't do shit to them w/o Spirit 5 (and even then there's a penalty). <br /> <br /> Maybe he can send the students to a Realm that's a twisted version of the school. I'm imagining something like Castelvania's inverted castle where the characters have to survive a supernatural situation w/o using magick. Alternatively, they have to use magick to fix a magical disaster caused by mirror students (a sort of &quot;in my shoes&quot; situation). As a spirit of a place where most magicks are Coincident (only get Paradox on a botch) probably he cares the most about overuse of magick and/or wanton breaking of the Earthly Foundations (that even the most radical Reality Zones have to respect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T07:38:35-08:00","id":1285562,"title":"","content":"How numerous are this school's teachers ? If there aren't many, I think this place could be regarded as problematic by some for giving a narrow or an incomplete representation to many Traditions and Paradigms, while creating an incorrect impression of variety and inclusiveness. There are many different Houses and methods in the Order of Hermes, great many Kamamargas and attitudes in the Cult of Ecstasy, many variations of theory and practice in the Virtual Adepts, and the Sons of the Ether, and different perspectives among the Verbenae. What guarantees does this school have that it's students won't come out with a too simple knowledge and perspectives in regard to different Traditions and Paradigms ? Won't students of a particular Paradigm be given limited choice of what methods and perspectives to learn ?<br /> <br /> What about Widderslaintes attending this school ? That is, if you are going with a version of the Nephandi that doesn't have Widderslaintes sooner or later betray every person they associate with who isn't a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> How many from among the Traditions would know about this school ? Would this school staff and students strive to make it known, or the opposite of this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:32:39-08:00","id":1285587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285562#post1285562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How numerous are this school's teachers ? If there aren't many, I think this place could be regarded as problematic by some for giving a narrow or an incomplete representation to many Traditions and Paradigms, while creating an incorrect impression of variety and inclusiveness. There are many different Houses and methods in the Order of Hermes, great many Kamamargas and attitudes in the Cult of Ecstasy, many variations of theory and practice in the Virtual Adepts, and the Sons of the Ether, and different perspectives among the Verbenae. What guarantees does this school have that it's students won't come out with a too simple knowledge and perspectives in regard to different Traditions and Paradigms ? Won't students of a particular Paradigm be given limited choice of what methods and perspectives to learn ?<br /> <br /> What about Widderslaintes attending this school ? That is, if you are going with a version of the Nephandi that doesn't have Widderslaintes sooner or later betray every person they associate with who isn't a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> How many from among the Traditions would know about this school ? Would this school staff and students strive to make it known, or the opposite of this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>- I'm planning to have quite a few Hermetics and Choristers (the school was only for Hermetics until the 1500s, and only for Hermetics and Choristers until the 1850s), and there will be fewer representatives of the other 7 Traditions yes. Some teachers will only visit the school a few times a year, and some students will have to rely on books written by members of their Traditions. However there should be at least one representative of each Tradition at the school.<br /> <br /> When you leave the school you are not finished learning as a Mage. You could leave with a completely average or stereotypical Etherite understanding and then develop a more complex or esoteric understanding later. The stated intention of the school is not to train perfect or ultimate mages, it's to keep vulnerable children safe. The school exists because of fear of the Technocracy. It could be argued that the true purpose of the school is to keep the world safe from the students however.<br /> <br /> Some students will have to rely on their own research and experimentation, and on other students, to get a robust understanding of their paradigm. It's far from perfect. It's very likely that any shamanic mage who leaves the school will immediately return to their homeland to reconnect with their roots and discover the lore of their people, and their view on spirits and shamanism.<br /> <br /> So yeah the school is not all things to all students, and would never claim to be. It's a safe environment where they can learn loads of useful stuff (a good chunk of which will just be improving Abilities). When an Etherite leaves with a solid scientific understanding and a very vanilla scientific paradigm they may later develop a completely different approach based off of that foundation.<br /> <br /> Some Mages whose relatives are studying at the school will be unhappy with the way their education goes since students are free to dabble as they like, and a Hermetic might be annoyed to find that their niece leaves the school with an understanding of magick that they don't approve of. However the Traditions have benefited from having this population of cooperative Mages who have broad understandings.<br /> <br /> - With regards to Nephandi, since there's no way of sensing them they will be a problem if they attend. However Mages tend to be sent to the school after they've attracted some attention, and if we're looking at a Widderslainte the most likely result is them being recruited by the Nephandi first. Furthermore Widderslaintes are very rare compared to normal Mages and like most Mages will awaken in adulthood, not childhood.<br /> <br /> But in spite of those slim odds a Widderslainte will have ended up at the school at some point. The lore of the school can include the one case where they've had to use the Gilgul rite on a student, but this has been buried within the school's history. Furthermore I might insert a Widderslainte into the PCs' midst, and let the events play out around them.<br /> <br /> - The school's existence is only known explicitly by those who have attended and those who have worked there. Otherwise the Council of Traditions simply has this understanding about that if you are dealing with a precocious Mage the safest thing to do is pass that information up the chain of command and let the Council take care of it. There are rumours about some sort of school and it's generally understood that child mages are better off there compared with the alternatives, which are death, recruitment by the Technocracy, recruitment by Nephandi, becoming a Marauder, or causing trouble among sleepers and drawing too much attention to Mages.<br /> <br /> Simply put the school wouldn't function at all if Mages weren't terrified of the Technocracy, and if there weren't horror stories floating around about Mages coming home to find their families killed or abducted by agents during a pogrom. Furthermore there are horror stories floating around about child mages losing control of their powers and they aren't pretty either.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy doesn't know that Anstruther exists because of its powerful Arcane rating. However it is aware that something like Anstruther *probably* exists since it has education facilities for precocious citizens. The same is true in reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:37:49-08:00","id":1285593,"title":"","content":"I'm also planning for the school to have hidden passageways leading to various chantries which are generally restricted for security reasons. Students will be able to gain access to them with special permission if they need to find a specific sort of mentor. It's very much the sort of thing you need to go to a committee to talk about and wait a few months for, so that the school can vet a potential mentor and check they're trustworthy, can keep the gateway to the school a secret etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:40:35-08:00","id":1285594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285544#post1285544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh...that's SO not going to work well for the student. And not only because Spirit 2 doesn't allow much control. The thing with Paradox Spirits it's that you can't do shit to them w/o Spirit 5 (and even then there's a penalty).<br /> <br /> Maybe he can send the students to a Realm that's a twisted version of the school. I'm imagining something like Castelvania's inverted castle where the characters have to survive a supernatural situation w/o using magick. Alternatively, they have to use magick to fix a magical disaster caused by mirror students (a sort of &quot;in my shoes&quot; situation). As a spirit of a place where most magicks are Coincident (only get Paradox on a botch) probably he cares the most about overuse of magick and/or wanton breaking of the Earthly Foundations (that even the most radical Reality Zones have to respect)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know that you need Spirit 5 to work on a Paradox Spirit, that's part of the reason I love them. It's especially hard with manifestations of Justice since he has a crazy amount of innate countermagick and will be extra cruel if you try anything on him.<br /> <br /> Paradox Realms as punishment is definitely good thematically, teach the PCs and their players to respect the universe. I could imagine them incorporating a bit of Wrinkle into it too. Let them watch what they just did from the outside, give them a chance to apologize and then do something different this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T10:36:39-08:00","id":1285604,"title":"","content":"The School has 5 houses. There were originally 4, one for each of the foundations of Hermetic theory.<br /> <br /> Anima (command over life)<br /> Vires (command over elemental forces)<br /> Corona (command over the mind)<br /> Primus (command over quintessence)<br /> <br /> When the Choristers were allowed to enter the school a 5th house was established, Saint Benedict's.<br /> <br /> In modern times there are students from across all the different Traditions, but the tradition of the school is very old and students are simply divided among these five houses. Hermetics always go into the first four and Choristers always go into the fifth, but otherwise students are divided between them. Each house has a motto, notable alumni, associated traditions (from songs to pranks)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T12:01:56-08:00","id":1285976,"title":"","content":"PC concepts are starting to roll in, and I have one question...<br /> <br /> One of the players wants to play a mage who is an artistic soul, and they imagine them doing magick using art and music. The kid is currently inept in these things but that's where room for growth comes in. This seems to fit best with the Cult of Ecstasy since they aren't religious. However they also love the stuff about lucid dreaming, the Dream background and the Demesne background. I'm keeping Lucid Dreaming at 0, Demesne at 1 and Dream at 1 since they're freshly awakened, BUT I'm wondering which Tradition is best associated with magick relating to Dreams, lucid dreaming and the high Umbra in general? The cult of ecstasy? The akashics? The verbenna?<br /> <br /> The other concept is &quot;Chosen One gone wrong&quot;. When he was a baby a counterspell sealed by his dying mother caused the death of a Nephandus who tried to murder him. This fulfilled a prophecy about him defeating the said Nephandus, who was widely feared and reviled. However this is his actual span as a chosen one done. Destiny had that role in store for him and it was completed when he was 1. Now he's 11 and he is certain that things can't be so closed and finished. He finds that he's mediocre compared to his peers, that he is far from exceptional in his studies. This all comes after a lot of &quot;we are expecting a lot from you young man&quot;. He just can't accept that he's normal, so he starts to do that thing some kids do where he lies to himself and others to inflate his value. The trouble is that he's a Mage and his neurosis is only getting worse with time. The player imagines that he may even go Marauder over it, with his own reality being one where he is the destined chosen on, and his reality sink being an effect which drags in bystanders into agreeing with him.<br /> <br /> I've decided to possibly take it a step further; his Manifest Avatar has taken on the form of this dead Nephandus. The Nephandus is 100% dead, no question, but his Avatar is mimicking him. This means that it can drive him on as the antagonist he is wishing for, the dark figure who will make him special, a figure he can seek vengeance against. The prophecy says he's special because this dark figure exists and he is destined to kill him; if the figure is still around then he's still special. If he ever does become a Marauder this figure will kill another student and start actually being a real threat. It's like with an arachnophobic Marauder. If they fear spider attacks people might get bitten by spiders (assuming they have the necessary spheres to create spiders, or dangerous illusions of spiders, or call upon existing spiders, or pull spider spirits into our world).<br /> <br /> So he acts as a subversion of chosen one plots essentially. Normal guy ruins his own life and everyone around him by trying to adhere to a prophecy that makes him important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T12:33:37-08:00","id":1285984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285976#post1285976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PC concepts are starting to roll in, and I have one question...<br /> I'm wondering which Tradition is best associated with magick relating to Dreams, lucid dreaming and the high Umbra in general? The cult of ecstasy? The akashics? The verbenna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dreams &amp; lucid dreaming:<br /> Dreams and lucid dreaming are an important aspect of many cultures supernatural cosmology. No mystical Tradition it's trully devoid of that: from prophets being taken in drams by angels to shamans entering the Dream Time, even Etherites should have a fond place of genius that happens in the dreams.<br /> <br /> If you don't want too much religion being tossed probably a Jungian Paradigm that searches archetypes in dreams or a Castaneda-esque new-age shamanism that practices Dreaming would work - that is, probably: Hermetic chaos mage, Hollow One, New-Age-Dreamspeaker. The Cult of Ecstasy could work too, albeit they tend to be more about experiencing with the body there's potent experiences to be found in dreams, and there's not a freer state of the mind than Dreaming - I'm actually a bit surprised that they aren't more related with dreaming practices.<br /> <br /> The high Umbra in general:<br /> Mages oriented to abstract tought and symbolism go here (Astral Videre) when they Step Sideways (albeit you can't get beyond the Vulgate this way). That is, the majority of mages that don't follow a deeply primal and visceral Paradigm. A Dreamspeaker that represents the ancient cultural roots of a native-american civilization won't go here, but a new-age sort could. Obviously mages oriented to Mind and Spirit have an easier time with matters relared to the HU, but other than that there's no restriction.<br /> <br /> What does the player want from Art &amp; Dreams? If its to inspire emotion, straigth Cultist. If it's Platonic Beauty and/or Perfection we could have a Hermetic or Akashick. If it's comunion with another world then Dreamspeaker is, and away with the conceit of them being the noble savage tradition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-08-2019, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T14:05:41-08:00","id":1286011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285984#post1285984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> The Cult of Ecstasy could work too, albeit they tend to be more about experiencing with the body there's potent experiences to be found in dreams, and there's not a freer state of the mind than Dreaming - I'm actually a bit surprised that they aren't more related with dreaming practices.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Many - if not the majority - Mages of the Cult of Ecstasy should definitely be considering resting and chillin' out after experiences to be a complex and important activity in itself. Also, the activities that Ecstatics do for pleasure and for Magick do seem as ones that would be distinctly more likely to lead to dreams more often, compared to activities of other Mages. This is because of the very open nature of the activities that Ecstatics would be undertaking ; both these who are part of their Kamamargas, and also other activites.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285604#post1285604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The School has 5 houses. There were originally 4, one for each of the foundations of Hermetic theory.<br /> <br /> Anima (command over life)<br /> Vires (command over elemental forces)<br /> Corona (command over the mind)<br /> Primus (command over quintessence)<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these houses of this school associated to any extent with the Houses of the Order of Hermes that they share areas of interest with ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T18:32:06-08:00","id":1286060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1285976#post1285976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've decided to possibly take it a step further; his Manifest Avatar has taken on the form of this dead Nephandus. The Nephandus is 100% dead, no question, but his Avatar is mimicking him. This means that it can drive him on as the antagonist he is wishing for, the dark figure who will make him special, a figure he can seek vengeance against. The prophecy says he's special because this dark figure exists and he is destined to kill him; if the figure is still around then he's still special. If he ever does become a Marauder this figure will kill another student and start actually being a real threat. It's like with an arachnophobic Marauder. If they fear spider attacks people might get bitten by spiders (assuming they have the necessary spheres to create spiders, or dangerous illusions of spiders, or call upon existing spiders, or pull spider spirits into our world).<br /> <br /> So he acts as a subversion of chosen one plots essentially. Normal guy ruins his own life and everyone around him by trying to adhere to a prophecy that makes him important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marauder mightbe the wrong way to take it. He may just be falling into a deep Quiet. Once he goes Marauder his story is pretty much over, but regular Quiets can manifest apparently real people and objects (called hobgoblins, though they can look like anything including the dead Nephandus) and eventually the Quiet can take things into mindscape territory. There's a lot more opportunity to explore what is going on in his head in that direction. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T03:57:46-08:00","id":1286140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1286060#post1286060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Marauder mightbe the wrong way to take it. He may just be falling into a deep Quiet. Once he goes Marauder his story is pretty much over, but regular Quiets can manifest apparently real people and objects (called hobgoblins, though they can look like anything including the dead Nephandus) and eventually the Quiet can take things into mindscape territory. There's a lot more opportunity to explore what is going on in his head in that direction.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can Hobgoblins become visible to others, or harm them? I was tending towards Marauder since it would make his own psychosis and fear into what looks like a villain; a figure that can use magick and harm others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T07:56:13-08:00","id":1286178,"title":"","content":"Yes, Hobgoblins can do both of those things. Hobgoblin is basically a catch all term for manifestations created by a Quiet that can affect reality. It is technically unclear if Hobgoblins themselves can cast magic, but that's academic as any spells you really need them to set off can also be hobgoblins. So the Nephandus appearing as a specter to other students and tricking them into releasing monsters is a valid hobgoblins. So are the monsters released for that matter, although given this is a magical school they could just as easily be real. The Nephandus appearing physically and stealing things for a ritual works too (as does the effects of the ritual itself). As does the Nephandus outright burning someone to death.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:22:57-08:00","id":1286216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1286178#post1286178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Hobgoblins can do both of those things. Hobgoblin is basically a catch all term for manifestations created by a Quiet that can affect reality. It is technically unclear if Hobgoblins themselves can cast magic, but that's academic as any spells you really need them to set off can also be hobgoblins. So the Nephandus appearing as a specter to other students and tricking them into releasing monsters is a valid hobgoblins. So are the monsters released for that matter, although given this is a magical school they could just as easily be real. The Nephandus appearing physically and stealing things for a ritual works too (as does the effects of the ritual itself). As does the Nephandus outright burning someone to death.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! That's really helpful, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:27:32-08:00","id":1287324,"title":"","content":"Had our session 0. It was very illuminating and interesting.<br /> <br /> Oliver; a bit of an anti-chosen one as I mentioned earlier. Devotional (Destined) and Static (Prophetic). Hermetic, with standard tools and practice. Wants so badly to be the chosen one, to the point where he has manifested his own personal antagonist as an Avatar. He is going to steal credit for things and use his Manipulation and Leadership to get people to believe in him as a chosen one. Furthermore the player has invested bonus points into Resonance and Synergy so he REALLY seems like a chosen one superficially.<br /> <br /> Rachael; a cyber-bully who runs the line between Virtual Adept and Euthanatos. Performs curses and blackmail using forums, social media, chaos magick... drawing runes with a graphic pad, digging through facebook profiles to find dirt... Her Avatar is a forum account which only she can interact with, her Sanctum is an abandoned computer room in the basement full of rot and broken equipment, her Familiar is a Virus spirit. She has a very very powerful Entropic Synergy. She's fond of fanfiction and cosplay, and while she is a nasty critic she does protect her friends up to a point. Think &quot;no one gets to bully my friends but me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finn; a budding herbalist who grew up on a farm. He has an Elemental (Verdant) and Dynamic (Growing) Res/Syn. His practice mostly involves preparing plant ingredients to make concoctions, and gardening, working with plants directly. He's a spiritualist, and has Willow as a Totem. He's just a lanky friendly kid who is probably going to be bullied at first. He has a Greenhouse as his sanctum, with a beehive in the roof as his Familiar.<br /> <br /> Derek; a dreaming clumsy stocky kid who wants to be dainty and artistic. When he dreams he can fly and dance and sing beautifully. Unbeknownst to him (and the player) his mother was a Fae Queen who died when he was young, making him Fae Blooded. I'm representing this with the Nephilim merit. He has a goldcrest bird as his Familiar (created by his mother in her dying moments to protect him; it is in fact some sort of fae), and has a Demesne. Temperamental and Devotional, with a focus on artistic flair and mood. The concept (art and dreams) is neatly tied together by the background (fae influence). He's painfully dyspraxic so his dreams of dancing and performing may be misguided, although music and art are still options. Performs magick through meditation, dancing, art, music... He's very strong and has a talent for fighting, but he really hates brawling and doesn't want people to be afraid of him.<br /> <br /> Ivan; a child from an island not found on any map. His tribe are descendants of Mimir himself, and their island has slipped away from our realm (midgard) with time, just as lands like Lemuria and Atlantis have, like Bygones. His tribe is full of mystics, and he has been sent away to form closer bonds with the Traditions, particularly the Verbena. Unbeknownst to him his family's greatest seers have also predicted doom befalling their isles, so sending away a few children seems like a safe move. He performs magick through god-bonding, and a sort of pagan spiritualism. He's a fish out of water in midgard, and will be a tad arrogant and out of place. Mimir acts as a &quot;Totem&quot;. He's very soft for his culture, preferring using a bow to melee weapons, and having little skill in combat.<br /> <br /> Since the characters are just starting they only have 3 dots in spheres and I limited the freebie point totals along with the base Ability totals (11/7/5 not 13/9/5). I also capped Abilities at 2, allowing only one level 3 Ability (whatever they're especially good at).<br /> <br /> I'm placing a lot of emphasis on Synergy and Resonance since the school is such a clusterfuck of mystical and technological paradigms, with an incredibly permissive (if volatile) consensus. Paradox might not get you, but magick still has consequences. Mess with the weather? Rain for a week. Too many people teleporting and conjuring? You step out of bed and into the lake. Ward your dorm against spirits? The Gauntlet across the school thickens, disrupting work everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-13-2019, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T06:39:53-08:00","id":1287517,"title":"","content":"Your comment on teleportation reminds me of some fun with altered internal dimensions once. The characters were entering a house they knew was spacially screwed up, so one of them had the bright idea to bring a rope and tie it to the handle of the front door in case they got lost. The thing was, I had already decided that I was going to roll to find out which room they ended up in every single time they passed through a door. The rope didn't make a lot of sense in that scenario, but instead of telling them that and coming up with some kind of BS reason why they'd know it didn't work I decided to toy with them. <br /> <br /> After a little while they entered a room they'd never been in and saw a rope stretched between two doors. Concerned they started following their rope back and sure enough it took them back through a different path than the way they had come (I don't remember if it took them to rooms they hadn't been in, but it could have). It was also far, far longer than it was when they tied it to the door. As they progressed they kept seeing the rope in increasingly odd paths through the rooms, and by the end they were having to crawl through a virtual spider web created by their own nigh infinitely long rope.<br /> <br /> This wasn't a Mage game, but it is the kind of thing I would consider pulling in the right circumstances in a Mage game. Specifically in a permissive but volatile consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:52:51-08:00","id":1287572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1287517#post1287517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your comment on teleportation reminds me of some fun with altered internal dimensions once. The characters were entering a house they knew was spacially screwed up, so one of them had the bright idea to bring a rope and tie it to the handle of the front door in case they got lost. The thing was, I had already decided that I was going to roll to find out which room they ended up in every single time they passed through a door. The rope didn't make a lot of sense in that scenario, but instead of telling them that and coming up with some kind of BS reason why they'd know it didn't work I decided to toy with them.<br /> <br /> After a little while they entered a room they'd never been in and saw a rope stretched between two doors. Concerned they started following their rope back and sure enough it took them back through a different path than the way they had come (I don't remember if it took them to rooms they hadn't been in, but it could have). It was also far, far longer than it was when they tied it to the door. As they progressed they kept seeing the rope in increasingly odd paths through the rooms, and by the end they were having to crawl through a virtual spider web created by their own nigh infinitely long rope.<br /> <br /> This wasn't a Mage game, but it is the kind of thing I would consider pulling in the right circumstances in a Mage game. Specifically in a permissive but volatile consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a neat idea with warped space. Correspondence and Time can both create very strange environments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T04:55:14-08:00","id":1288222,"title":"","content":"On reflection I've decided that the setting would benefit from a significant tweak to the EXP system in Mage. Split EXP into Mundane and Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> In the normal system I'd award 4 points of EXP after a session to all PCs (I don't like the systems in WoD where you give different EXP to different PCs), which they can spend on anything they like. The worry is that they'd tend to invest in Spheres, Arete and the &quot;cool&quot; backgrounds while neglecting their Attributes and Abilities.<br /> <br /> In this system I'd award 5 or 6 EXP after a session, split between Mundane (used to upgrade Attributes, Abilities, Willpower, purchase most Merits) and Arcane (used to upgrade Spheres, Arete, mystical backgrounds like Demesne, Resonance/Synergy, purchase supernatural merits...).<br /> <br /> This allows me to award more EXP without the characters growing as Mages too quickly. It also sticks to a core theme of Mage; magick is who you are, not just what spells you can do. A Mage's powers are supported and informed by their Attributes and Abilities.<br /> <br /> It also means PCs don't feel hampered when they invest EXP in stuff like Cooking and Theology. They have Mundane EXP that they need to use on something like that after all.<br /> <br /> Furthermore it allows me more fine-tuning control. I can decide that the PCs are too advanced in Spheres for their age and start to limit Arcane EXP to 1 point per session until some in-game time has passed. This way they continue to improve without being on a constant track to being archmages.<br /> <br /> e.g Finn gets 6 EXP after a session. 4 is Mundane and 2 is Arcane. They spend the 4 EXP raising two of their Abilities (Enigmas and Esoterica, describing how they spend time studying their notes from lessons on puzzle solving and magickal theory) and they save the remaining 2, since they don't have enough EXP to raise their Arete yet. Alternatively, they could spend that 2 EXP upgrading their Familiar Background rating. They describe cultivating new flowers rich in various types of nectar, to feed the hive and help it grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-15-2019, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:50:13-08:00","id":1288243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1288222#post1288222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection I've decided that the setting would benefit from a significant tweak to the EXP system in Mage. Split EXP into Mundane and Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> In the normal system I'd award 4 points of EXP after a session to all PCs (I don't like the systems in WoD where you give different EXP to different PCs), which they can spend on anything they like. The worry is that they'd tend to invest in Spheres, Arete and the &quot;cool&quot; backgrounds while neglecting their Attributes and Abilities.<br /> <br /> In this system I'd award 5 or 6 EXP after a session, split between Mundane (used to upgrade Attributes, Abilities, Willpower, purchase most Merits) and Arcane (used to upgrade Spheres, Arete, mystical backgrounds like Demesne, Resonance/Synergy, purchase supernatural merits...).<br /> <br /> This allows me to award more EXP without the characters growing as Mages too quickly. It also sticks to a core theme of Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>This...is actually such an utterly simple, yet great house rule. I love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> While normally the ST needs to extend a bit of manual oversight over what their players are investing the XP in, this kind of lessens the burden just a tad, and it actually makes quite sense from an 'in-game' perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T10:21:41-08:00","id":1288322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1288243#post1288243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This...is actually such an utterly simple, yet great house rule. I love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> While normally the ST needs to extend a bit of manual oversight over what their players are investing the XP in, this kind of lessens the burden just a tad, and it actually makes quite sense from an 'in-game' perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Another neat benefit is that there isn't a feeling of worry in character generation. At one point I felt like any points I didn't have in Computer after character gen I'd never be able to invest in later, since a dot in Computer costs say 6 or 8 EXP, and just a few more EXP gives me a dot in a Sphere. It made me feel like I needed to start with Computer 4 essentially, since any points in Abilities could produce so much more power if put into Spheres. With this system I can be confident that I'll have EXP for all my important skills, and I won't be falling behind the other PCs.<br /> <br /> Also it's kind of relaxing to be able to spoil my PCs with loads of EXP without worrying about what they spend it on. Attributes and Willpower are expensive enough to soak up a lot of Mundane EXP for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-15-2019, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:34:07-08:00","id":1288463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1287324#post1287324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Paradox might not get you, but magick still has consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>So characters at the school are less likely to accumulate Paradox Points due to using Magick ? Is this comparable or similar to how Sanctums of Mages work in regard to this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T03:49:13-08:00","id":1288566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1288463#post1288463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So characters at the school are less likely to accumulate Paradox Points due to using Magick ? Is this comparable or similar to how Sanctums of Mages work in regard to this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the school does have Sanctums of varying power. Naturally for a Sanctum to maintain its power it has to be at least somewhat private, so the common learning areas aren't Sanctums. The private Dojo of the Akashyana gym teacher where he inducts students into studying Do, however, is.<br /> <br /> The reason students tend to escape Paradox in the setting is that there are zero Witnesses in the entire academy grounds, and the local consensus is very permissive. As long as what you're doing makes sense within your own paradigm, you'll remain Coincidental essentially. You're wandering around a place where the response to pulling out a fireball is &quot;that's dangerous&quot; not &quot;that's impossible!&quot;. However if a person is just making up random bullshit (I, a naturalistic Verbena, am going to give this guy rabies through a voicemail message) then it will tend towards vulgarity.<br /> <br /> And of course, effects that are always Vulgar will still be Vulgar here.<br /> <br /> But the setting reduces the odds of accumulating Paradox quite considerably, is the take-home message.<br /> <br /> The after-effects of Resonance and Synergy however are another story. And if you are messing up local reality (even coincidentally) the &quot;Groundskeeper&quot; may want to have a stern word with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:48:18-08:00","id":1288607,"title":"","content":"A problem occurred to me; all the PCs are Arete 1 and may be stuck there for a while. Level 1 spheres mixed with Abilities are great for problem solving, BUT people come along to a magic setting expecting to be able to command magic.<br /> <br /> So I've decided to add a new feature to the school.<br /> <br /> High in the castle's graceful towers, among the spires of House Corona, there is a strange little storeroom holding a reclusive Mage. Samuel Hurt, master wandmaker. When first year students visit him he pairs them with an object that will act both as a channel for their powers (a Unique instrument) and as their first way of using advanced Magick.<br /> <br /> A Hermetic might leave with a wand that allows them to control one of the elemental forces, for example, with a Forces 2 effect bound into the Wand.<br /> <br /> All of the Wonders he makes are Hermetic naturally, and he's one of the most well-renowned creators of these wands and staves. If a student enters who is difficult to match with anything in his stock, he'll disappear through a door leading to a corridor (Corridor? We're at the top of a tower...), only to return seconds or hours later holding what the student needs.<br /> <br /> For example, for my Entropic Computer Expert he'll return with a sleek metal remote with a Data 2 effect that allows the bearer to forge a connection with something for the purposes of using their Abilities or Spheres. For example it could connect her to a computer to interact with it with Computer/Technology, or to cause havoc with Entropy 2 when she develops it.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the kids get a hold of something special to them early on that lets them do proper magickal stuff. Furthermore as they grow they will leave these objects behind, or find new and cool ways of using them (that flame control effect is much scarier when the wielder has Arete 5 after all).<br /> <br /> p.s. &quot;Samuel Hurt&quot; is a reference to John Hurt, who portrayed Olivander. It is in no way a reference to the infamous WoD Gary Stu by a similar name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-16-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:54:24-08:00","id":1288612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1288607#post1288607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem occurred to me; all the PCs are Arete 1 and may be stuck there for a while. Level 1 spheres mixed with Abilities are great for problem solving, BUT people come along to a magic setting expecting to be able to command magic.<br /> <br /> So I've decided to add a new feature to the school.<br /> <br /> High in the castle's graceful towers, among the spires of House Corona, there is a strange little storeroom holding a reclusive Mage. Samuel Hurt, master wandmaker. When first year students visit him he pairs them with an object that will act both as a channel for their powers (a Unique instrument) and as their first way of using advanced Magick.<br /> <br /> A Hermetic might leave with a wand that allows them to control one of the elemental forces, for example, with a Forces 2 effect bound into the Wand.<br /> <br /> All of the Wonders he makes are Hermetic naturally, and he's one of the most well-renowned creators of these wands and staves. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he make Wonders in the Hermetic style for non-Hermetic characters as well ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T09:02:39-08:00","id":1288615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1288612#post1288612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he make Wonders in the Hermetic style for non-Hermetic characters as well ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't bond with anything he has stored in this small circular store-room, he disappears as I described and returns with something fitting. Since he couldn't have possibly made them (they're not in his style), it's anyone's guess where he is getting them.<br /> <br /> Essentially everyone leaves with something they can work with. There's some overlap naturally; Choristers and Verbena have enough overlap with Hermetics in some places that some Wonders could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:41:20-08:00","id":1289246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1288607#post1288607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> p.s. &quot;Samuel Hurt&quot; is a reference to John Hurt, who portrayed Olivander. It is in no way a reference to the infamous WoD Gary Stu by a similar name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It should be, though. He was rescued from his eternal ashtray, but is now cursed to never be able to use the artifacts or powers that fall into his hands. <br /> <br /> One other thing you could do is let the players spend XP to gain partial access to level 2 spheres. They can't learn the Sphere entirely until they get to Arete 2 but they can buy a specific trick or two for a point of XP*. This would be narrowly tailored, not suited for improvisation and always carries restrictions that relate to the student's paradigm. So for instance, one mage might be able to cast a small fireball, but it will look like a small devil and always travel directly towards the nearest source of fuel. Another student might be able to hear a single 5 second piece of conversation from the past. Also these would still have the difficulty of Forces and Time 2 respectively, but the students would still cast <br /> <br /> *The experience point would also count towards learning the actual sphere, but that won't be possible til later.<br /> <br /> I've never considered Mages to be strongly aware of the numbers of the game. They are aware that leaps forward in capability are often preceded by bursts of understanding, but they aren't always aware of when that happens in others. So the teachers will still teach lessons that relate to the higher spheres even before the kids can actually understand them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T13:13:33-08:00","id":1289281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289246#post1289246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It should be, though. He was rescued from his eternal ashtray, but is now cursed to never be able to use the artifacts or powers that fall into his hands.<br /> <br /> One other thing you could do is let the players spend XP to gain partial access to level 2 spheres. They can't learn the Sphere entirely until they get to Arete 2 but they can buy a specific trick or two for a point of XP*. This would be narrowly tailored, not suited for improvisation and always carries restrictions that relate to the student's paradigm. So for instance, one mage might be able to cast a small fireball, but it will look like a small devil and always travel directly towards the nearest source of fuel. Another student might be able to hear a single 5 second piece of conversation from the past. Also these would still have the difficulty of Forces and Time 2 respectively, but the students would still cast<br /> <br /> *The experience point would also count towards learning the actual sphere, but that won't be possible til later.<br /> <br /> I've never considered Mages to be strongly aware of the numbers of the game. They are aware that leaps forward in capability are often preceded by bursts of understanding, but they aren't always aware of when that happens in others. So the teachers will still teach lessons that relate to the higher spheres even before the kids can actually understand them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't Certamen mean that &quot;measuring&quot; Arete is relatively simple? You either have 1 orb or 2, there's no 1.5 orb situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T18:42:20-08:00","id":1289372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289281#post1289281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't Certamen mean that &quot;measuring&quot; Arete is relatively simple? You either have 1 orb or 2, there's no 1.5 orb situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I really dislike Certamen. It operates off of the rules of the book rather than what makes sense in the world or what makes sense in the Mage's paradigm. I can understand it as a Hermetic way of approaching duels (I can see them believing in ten coherent levels of excellence, possibly) but not as something that actually measures understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T01:10:52-08:00","id":1289445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289372#post1289372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I really dislike Certamen. It operates off of the rules of the book rather than what makes sense in the world or what makes sense in the Mage's paradigm. I can understand it as a Hermetic way of approaching duels (I can see them believing in ten coherent levels of excellence, possibly) but not as something that actually measures understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, the Ritual Circle for the duel is Hermetic. So someone who doesn't believe in discreet levels of Excellence ranging from 0 to 10 can just say &quot;this is all being filtered through a hermetic understanding upon which the ritual is based&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:14:15-08:00","id":1289689,"title":"","content":"I've decided to add a new (very minor) faction to the Mage setting, loosely based off of a vivacious faction of do-gooders.<br /> <br /> <u><b>This post will have huge show/book-ruining spoilers for the Series of Unfortunate Events lore, so don't read this until after you've binge-watched the show I suppose?</b></u><br /> <br /> This highly secretive organization (who refer to themselves as Librarians) spans the Traditions, Technocracy and the Crafts. It is made up of individuals who are devoted to understanding history, literature, philosophy and so on. Valued skills include Research, Library Science, Esoterica and Occult, Science, Law, Medicine, Academics, Subterfuge, Empathy, Meditation...<br /> <br /> The mission statement of the organization is to form a cautious coalition between the wider sects through back channels. It has its origins within the Virtual Adepts; a small number of them valued freedom of information above all and only saw a peaceful future for humanity in a scenario where the Technocracy and Traditions were both reformed. As these Adepts were new members of the Traditions and old members of the Technocracy, this meant that a delicate operation of connection could begin. Thankfully some premeditation on the part of these proto-librarians meant that some of them had remained loyal to the Technocracy. The vague end-game of the Librarians is a world where mysticism and technology exist in some sort of harmony, with wisdom from all practices being available to future generations of Mages.<br /> <br /> The Librarians have been successful in slowly growing their ranks, developing sophisticated code behaviours and phrases, avoiding detection, and recommending some really amazing books. They haven't been successful in ending the Ascension War. However, if a setting includes a movement pushing for a &quot;Kinder, Gentler Technocracy&quot; then this group is partially responsible.<br /> <br /> Although it wasn't their intention, the Librarians have fostered an environment within their society where they are perfectly placed to develop their Arete and become potent Mages. The Librarians treasure books and therefore have access to a large body of Grimoires of all kinds. Librarians tend to be recruited from positions of lore-keeping, custodianship and so on, so the network is a powerful hub of excellence.<br /> <br /> A member of this faction has met one of the PCs, and is very very slowly drip-feeding them the ideals of the Librarians. She has provided him with a book and tasked him with finding the young Mage who will really benefit from reading it (another PC... a very simple puzzle since the book is full of fairytales on plants, and one of the PCs is a mystic focused on herbalism).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:43:51-08:00","id":1289877,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting hybrid of the Traditions and Technocracy there. I tend to view the Traditions as being for individual paradigmatic freedom, their ideal world being one where every person can determine what works for them. The Technocracy on the other hand is for a unified world with a single coherent way of doing things that works well for anyone. These Librarians seem to want a single coherent world, but one that contains multiple layers some of which are only available to those who dig deeper. <br /> <br /> What would you say their common blind spots are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:56:01-08:00","id":1289905,"title":"","content":"This looks like a lot of fun. <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that there could possibly be some sort of long standing Verbena association with the school, primarily from the really ritualized and traditionalist Gardeners of the Tree types, with the various scions of Pure Blooded &quot;We Can Trace Our Family Back to the Wyck&quot; lines standing in for the Slytherin style snobs. <br /> <br /> And there really should be a teacher who specializes in the instruction of etiquette, manners, diplomacy and Ars Cupitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:12:19-08:00","id":1289911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289877#post1289877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting hybrid of the Traditions and Technocracy there. I tend to view the Traditions as being for individual paradigmatic freedom, their ideal world being one where every person can determine what works for them. The Technocracy on the other hand is for a unified world with a single coherent way of doing things that works well for anyone. These Librarians seem to want a single coherent world, but one that contains multiple layers some of which are only available to those who dig deeper.<br /> <br /> What would you say their common blind spots are?</div> </div> </div> </div>The librarians want humanity to move into the future, but they don't want total homogeneity in reality zones. To them, it's completely fine if a coven of druids have a nudist mystic colony in the middle of a huge national park. They accept that it's a good thing if sleepers agree on a superficial consensus across most of reality (planes fly, cars work, medicine saves lives), but it's also good if people can &quot;supplement&quot; that reality with their own beliefs on religion, mysticism, ascetic practices, weird science...<br /> <br /> STRENGTHS:<br /> <br /> Technocracy: actively engaged with the real world, and looking towards humanity's future.<br /> <br /> Traditions: value diversity in belief and custom, and reject a singular consensus<br /> <br /> WEAKNESSES:<br /> <br /> Technocracy: reject individuality, seek to force their ideas on everyone for the &quot;greater good&quot;<br /> <br /> Traditions: the majority of Traditions Mages spend their lives accumulating knowledge and raising their Arete, but do nothing to help sleepers across their whole life. They take part in the Ascension War at best; cloistered and detached from the human race with some notable exceptions. At the absolute worst the Traditions are like the worst kind of economic/philosophical professors who spend decades locked away in their faculty arguing over the interpretations of Marx-Engels, and in their whole lives barely interact with any members of the working class or help them in any way.<br /> <br /> Arguably the Librarians have the strengths of both and have shed the weaknesses but... well sadly the fact that they have a tiny membership and hold very little power within the sects means that it's almost a moot point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-20-2019, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:15:44-08:00","id":1289913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289905#post1289905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks like a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that there could possibly be some sort of long standing Verbena association with the school, primarily from the really ritualized and traditionalist Gardeners of the Tree types, with the various scions of Pure Blooded &quot;We Can Trace Our Family Back to the Wyck&quot; lines standing in for the Slytherin style snobs.<br /> <br /> And there really should be a teacher who specializes in the instruction of etiquette, manners, diplomacy and Ars Cupitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea! I'll have Verbena who can trace their roots back to Morgana La Fae and that sort of thing. Snooty Hermetic kids, snooty Verbena kids, snooty Choristers... so many options ;-)<br /> <br /> That's something I hadn't considered! I'll think about adding a teacher of diplomacy and etiquette. What Tradition would you recommend for that? I could use one of my existing characters. I have an assistant archiver from house Shaea. He's middle eastern and has a background in egyptology, so &quot;knowing customs and greetings is important&quot; feels like a logical lesson from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:25:05-08:00","id":1289937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289913#post1289913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something I hadn't considered! I'll think about adding a teacher of diplomacy and etiquette. What Tradition would you recommend for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>House Jerbiton. It is essentially as much their 'thing' as fire is for House Flambeau.<br /> <br /> Alternately, House Tytalus, with the approach that mastery of verbal dueling is every bit as important as mastery of combat.<br /> <br /> Other possibilities include Akashic Shi Ren, especially priggish upper class Verbena, and Etherites insisting on maintaining Edwardian era manners. (This could easily turn into the equivalent of Hogwart's Defense Against the Dark Arts, with a different teacher each year.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:11:07-08:00","id":1291278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289937#post1289937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> House Jerbiton. It is essentially as much their 'thing' as fire is for House Flambeau.<br /> <br /> Alternately, House Tytalus, with the approach that mastery of verbal dueling is every bit as important as mastery of combat.<br /> <br /> Other possibilities include Akashic Shi Ren, especially priggish upper class Verbena, and Etherites insisting on maintaining Edwardian era manners. (This could easily turn into the equivalent of Hogwart's Defense Against the Dark Arts, with a different teacher each year.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes definitely going to have it change through the years. First year it's from the House Shaea librarian. Etiquette learned from decades of dealing with spirits and humans across the middle east, north africa, europe and the umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:16:19-08:00","id":1291280,"title":"","content":"So I've done a few bits and bobs with my players. Letting them choose classes. Mundane vs Arcane EXP seems to be working out quite well, thinking I'll keep the house rule.<br /> <br /> Players are bonding with characters with similar practices, including eachother. They're working together in ways that would be impossible if they were older and more set in their ways. They don't &quot;know it's impossible&quot;, so it's possible basically. Why shouldn't a would-be ecstatic and a norse-style verbena work together on an effect? The ecstatic builds a nice bit of arts and crafts to dangle and show them the way, and the verbena helpfully draws a rune representing the realm of Heimdall onto it. You can see why some in the Traditions love the school, and others find it horribly distasteful to have impressionable children mingling with other mages.<br /> <br /> One set of two PCs are sharing a sanctum that suits both of them. Another pair have very similar interest in plants but are keeping their Sanctums separate. However they're nearby, and I'm planning that as they upgrade the background they may bump into eachother and run into some conflict. The druid has found an old tree stump from a sacred grove in the hedge maze, along with some pieces of what was once a standing stone, all tucked away and hidden behind a path of thorns. Just over the hedge the herbologist works in his greenhouse with his bee familiars. They could learn a lot from eachother in time.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> I had a repeating corridor warped by Correspondence. Two PCs managed to learn Correspondence to escape by comparing notes and taking the advice of a 5 point familiar. A small bird brought the artistic PC scraps to make a piece of art with, metal hanging from strings so the metal dangles and spins and points in certain directions. I played around with it and told the Norse PC that he saw Heimdall's influence guiding the other PC as he figured out how to escape this corridor that just led back on itself while staying in a straight line. Since the PCs start with 3 dots in spheres and not 6 I'm going to be handing out some free dots in the first year, keeping track of who's had what so it stays even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-23-2019, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:16:30-08:00","id":1291282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1289689#post1289689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've decided to add a new (very minor) faction to the Mage setting, loosely based off of a vivacious faction of do-gooders.<br /> <br /> This highly secretive organization (who refer to themselves as Librarians) spans the Traditions, Technocracy and the Crafts. It is made up of individuals who are devoted to understanding history, literature, philosophy and so on. Valued skills include Research, Library Science, Esoterica and Occult, Science, Law, Medicine, Academics, Subterfuge, Empathy, Meditation...<br /> <br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this organization / faction only include Mages as it's members ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:06:24-08:00","id":1291306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1291282#post1291282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this organization / faction only include Mages as it's members ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the goal is to create a &quot;shadow coalition&quot; between sensible members of both sects, the main body is Mages. It's all about resolving the Ascension War and facing the big threats to humanity as a whole. However there will be unawakened members within the ranks of both the Technocracy and the Traditions. Furthermore, when you collect vast quantities of knowledge you will attract the attention of other supernaturals. I'm imagining that at least one of the Librarians is on friendly terms with a Kiasyd for example.<br /> <br /> So a strange bunch of supernaturals may be hovering around the edges, but that applies to almost any organization of mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T20:30:07-08:00","id":1293408,"title":"","content":"Great thread. I had a combat/noncombat XP divide for an Exalted game and it became a staple house rule in all future games.<br /> <br /> The game sounds quite interesting and I hope to see more updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 03-04-2019, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T06:22:50-08:00","id":1293726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1284949-making-a-new-mage-setting-anstruther-academy-for-young-awakened?p=1293408#post1293408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great thread. I had a combat/noncombat XP divide for an Exalted game and it became a staple houseful in all future games.<br /> <br /> The game sounds quite interesting and I hope to see more updates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Thus far the PCs have settled in (with one exception, one of the players hasn't finished building his PC and sadly seems disinterested, I think Mage is a tad heavy in terms of Crunch for him). They've found their Sanctums and other Backgrounds and established friendships and rivalries. I've introduced the villain of book 2 very early on so that it isn't really obvious when the mystery kicks off.<br /> <br /> Right now my idea is to have seven &quot;Stories&quot;, with each building upon the last in terms of conflict. The conflict of the first story is an exam disguised as a deadly situation with an insane teacher. In fact the PCs were never in danger at all. The conflict of the final story has an outline including a huge space station, arguments over the fate of the world, aerial battles... and at the midway point we have interactions with Norse gods and similar. One of the big themes is &quot;the remnants of the mythic era are almost gone, we're at the tipping point where it either comes back in some way or goes away forever&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-04-2019, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T16:00:08-08:00","id":1294909,"title":"","content":"5 PCs, including my own (there is a co-ST so we can both have PCs, which is fun!) visited the tallest tower and received gifts from a strange old man called Hurt. He seemed like he had known they would be coming for a long time.<br /> <br /> Legend has it that Hurt climbed up the tower 100 years ago, at least, and has never come down. All first years who visit him may ask for a gift. Those who suit the items he creates (he is a master of Wonder creation) are given one of his many wands and other magickal items. Those who lie outside of his understanding receive items he has collected through various means. Gifts from alumni, mementos from old friends, mysterious items sent by researchers, and items taken from Union operatives, among others. The tower is the tallest in the castle, but it is &quot;shorter on the inside&quot;, making it quick to climb.<br /> <br /> Oliver, the &quot;false chosen one&quot;, received some spiel about both his mother and the wand she received, and how he sensed it had been destroyed &quot;on a terrible night where many paths ended&quot;, and a very vague hint about the dark mage he 'defeated' when he was young. He was given an ivory wand called the Tabula Rasa that can erase memories. Hurt had given him several to try, and none had worked with him. Frustrated, he tried the wand our of curiosity. Just to see what would happen. He regretted it, remembering handing another bright-eyed young man such a powerful ivory wand (its twin), and later wishing he hadn't. He wanted to take it back but stopped himself. The twin of the wand, which hasn't been mentioned yet, can create false memories. Bearing the two wands gives a terrifying degree of control. It is only with the twin wand that Erebus was able to create such a large following, through his powerful command of memory, taking control of many Sleepers by giving them memories that inspire total unquestioning devotion, hence Hurt's regret.<br /> <br /> Finn, who is connected to plants, was immediately pegged as having &quot;something of Willow (his totem) about him&quot;. He received a willow wand that controls plants (Life 2). &quot;Most of my creations are more ordered and well behaved. This one got away from me, honestly. It shall suit you though.&quot; He talks about the items like they are his children, and strangely enough very few of the items share his Resonance or Synergy.<br /> <br /> Derek, who is a nervous artist, was described as &quot;strange, fae or weird even...&quot; by Hurt, foreshadowing his parentage. He disappeared through a trap door and returned soaking wet, holding a box. Inside was a paintbrush called Helen, which was impossibly beautiful. Golden wood, perfect hair at the tip... and when he experiments with it he will find that his paintings reveal the true nature of the subject.<br /> <br /> Ivan, who is Norse, was given a ring that another Seidr had gifted to Hurt many years before. &quot;This ring was given to me by a remarkably brave and bravely remarkable woman, who hailed from a tribe like your own. I know she would want you to have it.&quot; The ring is marked by the Goddess Freya and reveals the spirits of the middle umbra, especially those linked to nature, and allows communion with them, and minor command over them.<br /> <br /> Alexandria, the prototype of a synthetic human project aiming to design a tactical leader for a group of soldier units (synthetic mix of Matter and Life patterns), was given a pair of Tru-Shades liberated from a Union agent. &quot;Once held by the Technocracy, and now in the hands of the Traditions... I think these glasses will suit you quite nicely, Alexandria&quot; (symbolism!). Since she is a sleeper (she has Enhancements and Advantages to make up for this) their level 1 effects will help her immensely, allowing her to examine Life, Matter, Forces and Prime patterns through vision, as well as giving spatial coordinates (bearings and similar) via Correspondence, although only one aspect can be examined at a time. The glasses are very limited however, in the sense that they can only ever give 1 success' worth of information, and the senses can't be mixed.<br /> <br /> The other PCs will get their own items in their next session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-07-2019, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T07:53:00-07:00","id":1295817,"title":"","content":"Interesting session with a lot of inter-PC conflict. A lot of stuff happened that I didn't plan, but it seems to be improving the story in ways that I couldn't have planned!<br /> <br /> - Aisea (cyberbully computer gremlin, self-identified &quot;otaku&quot; who likes hacking things) and Jayden (neglected son of morticians, obsessed with death and subterfuge, has an attitude problem, very edgy) climbed up to see Hurt. Aisea received a sort of wand-remote that allows her to perform a Data 2 rote and connect with distant computer systems, so that she can use her Computer skill on them (or perform other sphere effects). Jayden received a tarot deck and a bag full of dice. The dice have an Entropy 3 effect which manipulates the outcome of random events like card draws, roulette spins etc to suit the user. The dice themselves are made from the bones of a man who cheated at cards, and have a Chinese origin. They're both leaning towards Virtual Adepts and Euthanatos respectively.<br /> <br /> - Aisea discovered that Oliver and Ivan had broken into her and Jayden's den, and confronted them about it. She lied and exaggerated what they had done (claiming they'd smashed up her computer gear) to create more conflict. She then decided to use her new toy to hack Oliver's phone and listen to his conversations. She overheard something quite critical. She also stole some money from his bank account, after discovering he had Resources 5, and purchased a bunch of junk food and computer gear. To respect the PC's backgrounds I've said that the bank can't explain the transactions and refund the missing money. A and J also have a go at cheating on online gambling, and make a few hundred pounds.<br /> <br /> - Derek, Oliver and Ivan are told by their housemaster that they're welcome to read any books in his office, except for those on the top shelf which are restricted*. When he's distracted they take one of the books and put its dust jacket over another book of a similar size (a clever plan I hadn't considered; this means it will take much longer for him to realize the book is missing). The book contains details of a powerful Wonder hidden in the school in the 1400s, and they put together an idea that the housemaster is trying to find the object and steal it, based on the fact that the other book he had on the shelf was a history of the school. This conversation is overheard by Jayden and Aisea, who are delighted to have something to blackmail them with. Alexandria discovers their secret and memorizes the books contents, and they all agree to hide the book somewhere safe so that the housemaster can't get it. Derek and Oliver both have dead parents, so they are very drawn to the story, which details a Wonder that can resurrect the dead.<br /> <br /> *the housemaster has done this knowing that they won't be able to resist being told they can't read something. His plan is for them to discover the Wonder's location; at first it will seem like he has an evil plot, but in truth it's all part of an obscure end of year examination.<br /> <br /> It's all been quite hectic, and the inter-player conflict has been very inventive and fitting. There's this feeling that in the end they'll all be good friends, but for now they're feuding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-11-2019, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T16:20:29-07:00","id":1297827,"title":"","content":"- The computer gremlin Aisea decided to edit and highlight Computers for Dummies and give it to Hurt, as a gift. He was so touched because students never give him gifts in return. She then offered to return once each week to help teach him; he says yes just because he lacks company really. Incredibly wholesome for such a dark and brooding character actually.<br /> <br /> - The Norse PC Ivan observes a Rubix Cube and decides to make his own invention; a wooden &quot;Runix Cube&quot; that is marked with letters of his alphabet, and the runes representing individual Gods, rather than being marked with colours. The idea is that you rearrange the moving parts and then the random result gives you the answer you're looking for (using level 1 spheres). I gave him a dot in Entropy for his creativity (since the PCs start with 3 dots in Spheres I'm giving them free dots for RP until they hit 6).<br /> <br /> - The false chosen one, Oliver, goes to his first proper lesson at the school with Ivan, Ancient Greek and Greek Classics. These lessons are taught under starlight because of star signs, and also ambiance. Also, Professor Anstruther is a Vampire who has been teaching at the academy for over 800 years, so he's &quot;busy in the daytime&quot;. They discuss theology, cosmology, the nature of Gods, the fae folk, human descendants of gods, Greek heroes, and the importance of language as a Hermetic foundation. It is then revealed (while they discuss respected bloodlines that Spirits will often recognize) that Oliver is a first cousin of a girl he has come to hate, and that their family has been split up for some reason, with him staying with his aunt and her staying with their grandmother, and neither of them hearing about eachother growing up. This is overheard by Aisea via the phone.<br /> <br /> - Alexandria reveals her Synthoid nature to Ivan and Oliver, as they settle into their new hangout. This is overheard by Aisea via the phone.<br /> <br /> - Alexandria is asked by Oliver to go over the irregularities in his accounts, and using Hypercram for Finance she realizes that Aisea was the thief/hacker.<br /> <br /> - Aisea and Alexandria discuss her wrongdoing, and Oliver invading her Sanctum, and can't quite agree on who should apologize. The two meet up with Ivan and start watching Aisea's favourite anime; they're interrupted by demands from Aisea's online Cult, who want her to do more of her creepypasta / stories that come true / forum magick stuff. She shows Ivan how she works, and lets him pick a random member of the forum. They investigate her using the Data 2 Wonder, and then using Spirit 1 / Mind 1. It turns out based on her social media and online &quot;aura&quot; that she's smitten, and about to go on a date with a guy. Aisea investigates the guy and it turns out he's a total creep, so she hacks further and it gets worse; he's a habitual liar and cheater. They both decide that the only right thing to do is DOX THE HELL OUT OF HIM via his Facebook and Email, sending all his misdeeds to everyone. She writes up a story about an internet vigilante called Thunderthighs, Net Warrior, who will always find and expose wrongdoers, and shares it with her Cult saying they have to share for one (1) luck. Good RP and many successes causes her grateful and impressed followers to invite their friends to join, raising the Cult rating to 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T05:19:52-07:00","id":1298563,"title":"","content":"The players had a confrontation with a rather dangerous third year, in which they refused to show him the respect he demanded as a hereditary Peer (for those of you who don't know the UK, our House of Lords has people who are there because they inherited a title) and as a well-respected member of a dynasty of Mages. This culminated in the Norse PC spitting in his face, feeling his own honour was besmirched (I'm a god, I don't bow to children of weak and effete houses), and this led to a fight where the PCs escaped with some bruises, and a deep cut on the Norse PC's face.<br /> <br /> The peer in question is descended from a long lineage of Hermetic/Ecstatic Magi who are strongly linked to the Art of Desire. Debauchery, poetry, art, the Classics... they run the line between the Hermetic and Ecstatic principles. It is rumored that the lineage originated with some sort of tryst between Bacchus, the first Duke, and his wife, resulting in their son being metaphysically blessed by the god of Wine, Death, Carousing and Fertility.<br /> <br /> After the session my co-ST sent this to the players:<br /> <br /> In a deep dungeon of Vires, there\u2019s a cosy velvet room, with a roaring fire. In the middle, Lord Phillip paces the room.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat little peasant. He got me riled. You know what that means, Doyle?\u201d<br /> \u201cUh, That...um no?\u201d<br /> The other boy speaks up \u201cIt means that we\u2019re in trouble, His Lordship struck the ingrate and left a mark\u201d<br /> \u201cRaab is right, we need a way to mitigate the repercussions\u201d<br /> <br /> He thinks so a moment, before swinging his cane around and pointing it at Doyle <br /> <br /> \u201cTell me, Doyle, do you like froie gras, beluga caviar and champagne?\u201d<br /> \u201cI can\u2019t say I\u2019ve had the pleasure my Lord?\u201d<br /> \u201cHere\u201d he pulls out a dusty bottle and uncorks it. He then waves his hand over it and says<br /> \u201cThe god of wine commands you... let us taste heaven without the mark of drunkenness\u201d<br /> He then pours three glasses of the champagne.<br /> <br /> \u201cHere, a toast to Doyle\u201d<br /> \u201cUh, my Lord, why are we toasting to me?\u201d<br /> \u201cWell, Doyle, you\u2019re about to do me an immeasurable favour. And as such I will repay you by indulging your senses in the finer things in life\u201d<br /> <br /> He takes a sip and put down his crystal coop glass<br /> \u201cNow Doyle, do you remember what happened when we met those first years?\u201d<br /> \u201cUh.. yes?\u201d<br /> \u201cGood\u201d he slips on a set of white gloves and approaches Doyle<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll recall that that Norse boy, he was overcome by some berserker rage and he just LASHED OUT at you\u201d he swings a fist connecting directly with Doyle\u2019s chin<br /> \u201cHis friends did all they could to hold him back\u201d<br /> A left hook comes around and slams into the boy\u2019s eye<br /> \u201cAnd we tried to stop them\u201d as he says the word stop he kicks in Doyle\u2019s knee, a horrible crunch ringing out. He covers the boy\u2019s mouth with his hand so he can\u2019t scream out<br /> \u201cAll I could do was swing in my dear friend\u2019s defense, grazing his cheek, but snapping him out of his rage\u201d<br /> He places his other hand on Doyle\u2019s jaw and presses them in together; CRUNCH<br /> <br /> \u201cBut not before he savaged our poor friend Doyle\u201d<br /> <br /> Phillip steps back and admires &quot;Ivan\u2019s&quot; handiwork. He lifts up the coop glass to his friend\u2019s mangled face<br /> \u201chere you go old chum, now lets get you to the hospital wing\u201d<br /> He holds his hand over his head and says \u201cThe god of wine commands you: sip of this ichor and feel no pain\u201d<br /> He then calls Raab over and holds his hands over both of their foreheads<br /> \u201cThe god of wine commands you, drink of this heavenly mana and remember the confrontation as I have said it\u201d<br /> <br /> He begins to help Doyle up<br /> \u201cCome now Raab, lets get our friend some medical attention. It's a mark on my honour that I allowed such a brute to harm him...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T07:52:28-07:00","id":1313125,"title":"","content":"Update: So various things have come up. Characters have encountered their Avatars, knowingly and unknowingly. They're gradually heading towards the point where they'll start having their first seekings.<br /> <br /> And I've had a great idea for the events of the third year which I wanted to share. I'll do a tl;dr with the &quot;cool ideas&quot; since this will be quite long.<br /> <br /> Important details:<br /> <br /> - one PC is fae blooded, and their mother was someone important within the Arcadian hierarchy. They don't know this yet.<br /> <br /> - another PC is connected to the Norse Gods, and they never shut up about it.<br /> <br /> Plot:<br /> <br /> - Our fae-blooded PC starts having nightmares which intensify over time until they find they can't wake up, essentially entering a coma. These nightmares are taking place in what was his Demesne, but it has been invaded by monstrosities. Eventually the other PCs are able to connect into these dreams and help him survive and explore.<br /> <br /> - The PC finds that the wider world of Arcadia is ruled over by a single despotic Queen called Umbra, who has supplanted the old order, where there were four monarchs. Her armies of true fae (your elves and faeries, tall and beautiful and harsh and cruel) harness nightmares as steeds and cannon fodder, and suppress those who would resist the order of the Queen. The world is very slowly freezing over. He explores this world with the other PCs joining him via his astral link to the high umbra.<br /> <br /> - Throughout the lands there are rumours of the return of Aurora, the good and noble queen who left many years ago and did not return. The stars themselves did, briefly, arrange themselves to celebrate her return. Umbra was displeased with this and the relevant stars have been tortured and killed for their heresy. This is why the night sky is obscured in most places by a freezing mist; to hide the constellations and try to stifle hope. This is because the fae-blooded PC is the heir of this Queen, and many of the inhabitants of Arcadia can sense this. They are incredibly hopeful at first, and then bitterly disappointed when they meet this awkward human boy, little more than a dreaming child. There are themes of legacy and living up to your parents, with motherhood already being an overarching theme of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> - The PCs learn that Umbra is taking delivery of many different kinds of beings, from all sorts of realms. Bygones like centaurs and dragon eggs, rare spirits, and unusual imaginings from various parts of the high umbra. Humanity's greatest dreams and worst nightmares, plucked from their minds and brought to her great menagerie for some (presumably dark) purpose.<br /> <br /> - Eventually this all comes to a head when the PCs, perhaps accompanied by a small army of rebels, come face to face with Umbra. She simply laughs and warps all of the PCs (except for the fae blooded one) into horrible shapes, making them experience agonies beyond imagination for a brief moment. &quot;You are naught but dreams. Be gone from my realm, children.&quot; They all awaken in their beds, and find that no matter how hard they try they cannot return to the dreaming, or connect to the trapped PC's mind at all.<br /> <br /> - A prisoner, but free to explore Umbra's castle, the PC witnesses all the preparations Umbra is making for some coming calamity. Freezing and storing all sorts of beings. She claims that she needs to end the line of summer so that Arcadia can freeze over entirely. As long as he exists that can't happen. And she needs to do that so that she can preserve a &quot;seed bank&quot; of sorts. She has seen the end coming. Humanity will choke itself on fumes, or consume itself in a nuclear Armageddon, or awaken some ancient evil that will devour it (whether that means Vampires, Demons or Archmages she cannot say). She has given up hope on this reality, and simply wants to survive the coming destruction to populate whatever world comes next. Freezing and hardening her realm improves the odds of these creatures living to see the next reality (juxtapose this with a unicorn wandering around her palace courtyard with its foals to show where she's coming from). It's a sort of conservation / apocalypse survival setup.<br /> <br /> - Umbra discovers that the only way to kill the PC is to destroy his physical body, and she finds that his astral form is largely resilient to her powers due to some hidden protection. The other PCs, back in the real world, try and figure out a way to reach Arcadia. The Norse PC, guided by his Totem/Avatar/Gods will realize that they need to sail into the waters of Asgard (physically crossing into the high umbra proper, which is only possible because he is linked to that realm), and request the aid of his ancestors. From there Heimdall can tell them how to reach the Dreaming below. There's this whole journey into the High Umbra, a feast in Asgard with actual Norse gods and Valkyries, lots of amazing setpieces. They're told that Arcadia has been sealed off from outsiders, meaning there's no way in. Except one...<br /> <br /> - The only current opening into Arcadia is via a sort of delivery system that Umbra is demanding. There's a place in the high umbra with many names (some call it Pandemonium or the Nightmare Brood) where people's night terrors take form. If you dream about a horrible spider monster, it's born into this unending maelstrom of monstrosities. Umbra is taking delivery of these creatures since they form an important facet of her armies, and she believes that when the world ends Arcadia will come under attack no matter how well she hides the realm. She wants her soldiers riding on the backs of selectively bred night terrors that can cut through any force of demons or dark spirits. There is a &quot;port&quot; of sorts connecting the two realms, so the only way in is to survive passing through a gauntlet of terrifying monsters.<br /> <br /> - Umbra's plan to kill the PC's physical body is to open a portal in the Anstruther grounds which once linked Arcadia and the physical world &quot;when the stars were right&quot;. Of course many Hermetic scholars have shown that even when the stars take the right positions the portal cannot be opened, not realizing that this refers to the position of stars on both sides of the divide. She orders loyal stars to take the right formation, and as the portal opens she releases soldiers and nightmares into the grounds, ordering them to kill the sleeping boy. If any PCs have stayed behind at the school they'll get caught up in this. This creates some time pressure and urgency in the story.<br /> <br /> - There's a final battle within the skies of Arcadia, where the PCs are physically present and so Umbra can't simply banish them like before. The fae-blooded PC assumes the fae mien that was hidden within him at some critical moment, they manage to defeat Umbra or convince her to surrender. The final battle is yet more glorious setpieces; riding on frozen clouds, falling off waterfalls, battles in the crumbling ruins of the old castles.<br /> <br /> - BIG DECISIONS. What do the PC's learn from Umbra's plan, and her fears? How do they feel about her predictions, and what do they do with all these bygones they have now? What does the fae-blooded PC do with the fact that to many he's now King, or at least some sort of Prince, of Arcadia? He might reject his royalty and tell them to elect leaders or choose a good and noble King. Or he could accept his lineage and decide to rule this place in his dreams. What do they do with the portal? Destroy it? Let it stay open? It's the first time something like this has existed in many centuries. If it stays open bygones will be able to return to the world. The grounds of Anstruther are the perfect place for centaurs and unicorns to furtively test the waters of earth again. There could be this feeling that the mythic age will return, that technology won't rule the world forever, and that the monopoly of the Technomancers could be reversed.<br /> <br /> tl;dr, list of cool stuff<br /> <br /> - evil angry fae warriors riding on top of monsters from the nightmares of humans, that they've captured and trained and bred to inspire fear and be good mounts.<br /> - big epic setpieces like the feasting halls of Arcadia, the rainbow bridge, gods like Tyr and Heimdall and Mimir, plus a fae world which has something of a Narnia vibe.<br /> - the villain is doing bad things, but there's a legitimate thought process behind it and it's coming from a place of hopelessness, not pure evil. She's trying to create a spiritual Noah's arc so that when a new world is born the wonders of the old one won't be lost forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}